class.description:
The server reads the [NetwPersistenceConfig] and saved properties when [method Netw.spawn] returns the root, or when a root that was not spawned is ready. Wait for [signal loaded] before using stored values.
[codeblock]
@onready var entity: NetwEntity = NetwEntity.of(self)

func _ready() -> void:
    entity.persistence.loaded.connect(on_loaded)

func on_loaded(_found: bool) -> void:
    show_contents()
[/codeblock]
[method NetwPersistenceConfig.interval] saves changed values automatically. Freeing the root saves one last time, unless it never entered the tree. Failed loads and saves emit [signal NetwDatabase.failed].
